# PONS $101 — MASTER AGENT SPECIFICATION & BUILD ROADMAP

This is the master implementation specification for the PONS $101 — ROB Lab.

It converts the research architecture into an engineering program that authorized developers and agents—including @hashwarlock-operated agents—can execute systematically.

The target is not merely:

A TOKEN LAUNCHER.

The target is:

A REPRODUCIBLE TOKEN-LAUNCH RESEARCH FACTORY.

The completed system should be capable of:

• creating registered experiments
• preparing token metadata
• checking current network state
• validating Pons-compatible launch configuration
• generating unsigned launch payloads
• enforcing the human release gate
• reconstructing executed launches
• indexing early trades
• calculating fee components
• detecting repeated behavioral patterns
• producing mixed-methods research records
• preserving evidence
• tracking creator entitlement
• verifying treasury receipts
• generating research releases
• supporting independent replication

The governing question remains:

WHAT DID WE KNOW BEFORE THE OUTCOME?

